Package: statematch
Type: Package
Title: Match Messy US State Names and Abbreviations
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Ben", "Jefferies", email = "bjjefferies@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Converts free-text US state names, postal abbreviations and common
    variants (for example "N. Dakota", "Washington D.C.") to standard state
    abbreviations, full names and FIPS codes. Small misspellings such as
    "Tenessee" or "Pennsylvnaia" are corrected with a transposition-aware edit
    distance, and ambiguous input (for example "Mis") is returned as
    missing rather than guessed. Written in base R with no dependencies.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Depends: R (>= 3.5.0)
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.1
